**Compare**:
- 3V3 pin ≈ 3.3 V; 5V pin ≈ 5 V − 0.3 V ≈ **4.7 V**;
- LED current = (3.3 − 1.8) V / (330 + 25 + 12) Ω ≈ **4.1 mA** (25 Ω is the pin's output resistance, 12 Ω the LED's);
- pin voltage = 3.3 V − 25 Ω × 4.1 mA ≈ **3.20 V**; from this the output resistance ≈ **25 Ω**;
- pulled-up input: released reads high, pressed reads low (pressed, the button ties the pin to GND and 3.3 V / 45 kΩ ≈ 73 µA flows in the pull-up).
